# MLD (igmpd -6): an MLDv1 report and an MLDv2 report each make an IPv6
# group, keyed on its 33:33 MAC with the host and the PON as members; a
# refresh changes nothing; an MLDv1 done shortens the membership to the
# last-member time (no immediate leave), and an MLDv2 TO_INCLUDE of nothing
# does the same. The IPv4 table is untouched by any of it, and the IPv6
# state file lists the groups.
0 policy
snooping=1
igmp_function=0
immediate_leave=0
end
0 tick
1 mld1join 1 0 fe80::2 ff3e::8000:1
2 mld2join 1 0 fe80::2 ff15::1234
3 mld1join 1 0 fe80::2 ff3e::8000:1
4 state
10 mld1done 1 0 fe80::2 ff3e::8000:1
12 tick
13 mld2leave 1 0 fe80::2 ff15::1234
15 tick
16 state
